From 4f924250a2e906e0471388fce82b7e465ac42ef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:26:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the PREPTRACK Study Timer: focus workspace, study log,
 study hours
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ports the Study Timer section from PREPTRACK to this app's stack (plain
ES modules, no framework, no build step), keeping the reference behaviour
and adapting it to the local-first architecture here.

Screens
- #/timer — flip-clock focus workspace: Pomodoro (25/30/45/50/90-minute
  blocks with short/long breaks) or stopwatch, task line, live tab title,
  fullscreen stage, three atmospheres (woodland leaves, rainfall, night sky
  with meteors), ambience and a mindfulness bell. Finished blocks log
  themselves; early stops log what was actually worked; a manual log covers
  study that happened away from the timer.
- #/hours — the record: streak, this week vs last, average per active day,
  target met, a 26-week consistency heatmap and the weekly rhythm.
- Dashboard gains a "Studied today" figure in its standing strip.

Engine and data
- services/study-timer.js owns the clock independently of the screen, so a
  block keeps running while the reader is elsewhere. Time is anchored
  (anchorElapsed + anchorAt), so a throttled tab or a closed laptop cannot
  make it drift; state is mirrored to localStorage and restored at boot,
  with a phase that ran out while the app was closed closed out exactly once.
- services/study-log.js writes into the existing `sessions` store, so the
  timer's work is ordinary study time: the same rows feed the planner,
  backup/restore and the dashboard. Sessions carry session_type, task_name
  and completed; only finished focus blocks count as study minutes.
- Study days start at 4 AM (applicationDayKey in core/util.js), so a session
  past midnight belongs to the evening it began. todayKey() still reports
  calendar days, because exam dates must not move at 4 AM.
- Log-once guarantee: block ids already written live in localStorage, so a
  duplicate tick or a second tab cannot double-count a finished block.

Audio
- The reference shipped 38 MB of looped MP3s. Ambience and bells are
  synthesised with Web Audio instead (shaped noise through a filter plus a
  slow LFO; bells from decaying partials), so the section adds no download
  and offline use is untouched. Every audio call is a no-op where Web Audio
  is unavailable.

Housekeeping
- css/focus-timer.css holds the stage, clock, atmospheres and heatmap; its
  Night palette lives in one token block, so no literal colour escapes into
  a component rule.
- New files are precached in sw.js (VERSION bumped) and measured by the
  density guard; navigation, ⌘K and the tab bar carry the new destinations.
- tests/study-timer.test.js: 30 tests over the 4 AM rule, manual-log
  composition, the log-once and restore paths, phase transitions, settings
  clamping, and the rendered screens (budget, clock digits, atmospheres).

Full suite: 450 pass / 27 fail. The 27 failures are pre-existing and
unchanged (this checkout ships 1,300 of the 1,684 expected bank questions).
